  "confidence": "high",
  "review_flags": [
   "multi_zone_group",
   "or_branch_modelled",
   "verified_in_game"
  ],
  "notes": "CORRECTED after in-game verification by the user. The page does NOT state this and my first reading got it wrong: Yoran-Oran does not demand one specific item per run. ANY of the five listed items, from ANY of the listed monsters, completes the quest. That is ground truth from play, not from the page, and it is flagged verified_in_game so a later re-read of the wiki does not silently 'correct' it back.\n\nThe first authoring also had a real bug: all five monsters sat on ONE step carrying ONE zone (West Sarutabaruta), so the four that live elsewhere were indexed against a zone they never appear in and could never be marked. They are now five steps with their own zones, sharing a group, because picking which one to farm is exactly an unordered choice.\n\nEach monster drops more than the single item recorded against it -- Mandragora and Pygmaioi both drop three of the five. Only one item per step is recorded because duplicate evidence across two steps of one quest is a hard gate: the mark would jump to the later step the instant you obtained it. Every pairing written here is one the page's own table supports.\n\nThe engine cannot express an OR anywhere, so the turn-in carries no item list and shows grey rather than a wrong yellow. Cornette is deliberately the LAST group member: `best` is the highest evidenced step, so holding a Cornette -- the item players actually farm, ~60 of them to max Windurst fame -- is what lands the marker back on Yoran-Oran. Holding one of the other four leaves the marker on the monsters, which is a missed signal rather than a wrong one.\n\nUPDATED once the schema gained alternatives. The five items are now a single ev_alt list on the LAST group member, so holding ANY of them advances the ladder to the turn-in, and items_alt on the turn-in itself makes it go yellow. The earlier version had to pin one item per monster and only the last one led back to Yoran-Oran; that workaround is gone. Each monster still drops more than the item once recorded against it -- the pairings came from the page's own table.\n\nMoved out of the player-facing step notes (build vocabulary; see AUTHORING.md, 'Two notes, two audiences'):\n  step 6: Also buyable from Harmodios in Bastok Markets (K-10) when the nation places 1st or 2nd in Conquest, or from a Records of Eminence NPC for 50 sparks.",
